WEBVTT

00:02.212 --> 00:05.513
Charlottesville! You have been absolutely

00:05.613 --> 00:09.855
beautiful tonight! I know exactly what you were

00:09.895 --> 00:12.596
thinking when you bought these tickets. A bunch

00:12.636 --> 00:14.497
of stubborn ironheads marching into the

00:14.537 --> 00:18.518
Chancellery. You expected us to come out here

00:18.558 --> 00:22.860
bleeding maroon, right? But tonight, we aren't

00:22.920 --> 00:26.662
rivals. We're all just chasing the exact same

00:26.782 --> 00:32.160
signal. And for the record, your acoustic

00:32.200 --> 00:34.942
baffling in this arena is mathematically

00:35.022 --> 00:39.524
perfect. You have a very structurally sound

00:39.584 --> 00:43.726
home. She's not wrong!

00:45.847 --> 00:49.249
Listen, back on the Neon Hearts tour, we were

00:49.269 --> 00:52.271
just an opening act. We had family friends

00:52.331 --> 00:54.852
headlining, and they wanted us to jam with them

00:54.892 --> 00:58.876
to close the night. The label executives said,

00:59.037 --> 01:02.150
absolutely not. They kept us in our 30 minute

01:02.190 --> 01:06.402
box. Well, tonight, we call the shots. We don't

01:06.442 --> 01:08.944
do traditional opening acts anymore. If we're

01:08.984 --> 01:11.346
closing down the Chancellery, we're doing it

01:11.366 --> 01:14.608
with family. Two drum kits, two sets of

01:14.668 --> 01:19.212
instruments, everyone on the floor! We slipped

01:19.272 --> 01:21.674
a new song into the middle of our sets this year.

01:22.154 --> 01:24.916
We never announced it. We never said a word about

01:24.976 --> 01:28.179
it. But you've been screaming the lyrics back at

01:28.239 --> 01:31.500
us every single night. But I have a confession to

01:31.540 --> 01:34.381
make. We didn't write it. We just kept it warm.

01:34.941 --> 01:37.482
Tonight, we brought the architects out here to

01:37.522 --> 01:40.222
play it with us. You didn't have to look far to

01:40.262 --> 01:42.743
find them either. They built this engine in a

01:42.783 --> 01:45.884
garage right here off Route 29!

01:46.324 --> 01:49.665
Charlottesville, meet your hometown heroes!

01:50.305 --> 01:51.425
Crimson North!

02:29.654 --> 02:33.517
The static clears, the room is standing still

02:36.327 --> 02:41.772
We calculate the angles, bending time and will.

02:42.593 --> 02:46.597
I draw the line across the open air. No sudden

02:46.617 --> 02:50.701
moves, I know exactly where. We're taking off,

02:51.542 --> 02:55.766
but first we need the key.

02:57.608 --> 03:01.699
I call the coordinates out loud. A steady voice

03:01.719 --> 03:05.827
above the crowd, I hold my hand out, wait for the

03:05.847 --> 03:08.712
command, the double tap upon my hand, we never

03:08.773 --> 03:13.732
launch without the green light. We are charting

03:13.792 --> 03:17.713
the flight path perfectly aligned Leaving the

03:17.913 --> 03:21.654
gravity far behind We carry the weight We

03:21.714 --> 03:25.315
balance the load Following the numbers in the

03:25.395 --> 03:31.676
silent code Shoulder to shoulder Synchronized

03:32.257 --> 03:38.258
and true I'll always share the flight path

03:48.357 --> 03:52.481
The naval clock is ticking in my head. We take the

03:52.521 --> 03:55.923
leverage, nothing left unsaid. An anchor

03:55.963 --> 03:59.846
grounded firmly on the floor. We rise together,

03:59.907 --> 04:03.189
breaking through the door. The heavy crane is

04:03.409 --> 04:05.631
ready on the line.

04:09.453 --> 04:13.759
Call the coordinates out loud. A steady voice

04:13.919 --> 04:17.464
above the crowd. I hold my hand out, wait for the

04:17.505 --> 04:20.329
command. The double tap upon my hand. We never

04:20.369 --> 04:25.259
launch without the green light. We are charting

04:25.319 --> 04:29.141
the flight path perfectly aligned Leaving the

04:29.461 --> 04:33.082
gravity far behind We carry the weight We

04:33.162 --> 04:36.723
balance the load Following the numbers in the

04:36.823 --> 04:43.065
silent code Shoulder to shoulder Synchronized

04:43.205 --> 04:52.428
and true I'll always share the flight path with

04:52.468 --> 04:57.952
you When the system overloads and the signals

04:57.972 --> 05:00.574
start to fray We build a fortress on the ground to

05:00.614 --> 05:04.096
keep the storm at bay A heavy blanket in the dark,

05:04.116 --> 05:06.437
the pressure brings you home You'll never have

05:06.477 --> 05:09.739
to navigate the atmosphere alone

05:27.548 --> 05:29.989
Putting the flight path perfectly aligned,

05:30.369 --> 05:34.450
leaving the gravity far behind. We carry the

05:34.510 --> 05:38.110
weight, we balance the load, following the

05:38.190 --> 05:44.172
numbers in the silent code.

05:44.192 --> 05:49.193
The flight path is clear. The anchor is here.

05:50.933 --> 05:54.034
Double tap. We are clear to fly.

05:58.023 --> 06:03.428
Double tap! Reaching for the sky!

06:09.914 --> 06:11.475
Thank you Charlottesville!

06:13.537 --> 06:17.321
The Stardust Engine and Crimson Node love you!

